APPLICATION LAYER

The application layer of the OSI model is the layer that you will be most familiar with. This familiarity is because the application layer is the layer in which protocols and 
rules are in place to determine how the user should interact with data sent or received.

Everyday applications such as email clients, browsers, or file server browsing software such as FileZilla provide a friendly, Graphical User Interface (GUI) for users to interact
with data sent or received. Other protocols include DNS (Domain Name System), which is how website addresses are translated into IP addresses.
